# Tank Board I (003110) -- netlist converted from MAME
#
# Tank is two boards with no CPU. MAME's netlist (nl_tank.cpp) describes both as one circuit
# at the pin level, on one grid of designators -- but the boards each have their own grid,
# so Board I's D11 is not Board II's D11. This file is the part of MAME's circuit the sheets
# put on Board I, with every net that crosses to the other board landing on the cable
# contact Board I's sheet prints for it (Board I J1/J2 to Board II J4/J5).
#
# MAME's passive designators carry suffixes it added to tell the boards apart (R53A, R48B,
# C33C, R4V, R102MX, R74M1); they are stripped here, so the designators are the sheet's.
# Where a part's board was in doubt, the sheets decided: MAME's "A" mostly means Board I's
# sheet 2, but R8A-R11A and R37A are Board II's.
#
# Board I: tank and shell motion (sheet 1); coin logic, the play timer, the antenna, noise,
# shot and boom sounds and the audio mixers (sheet 2).
#
# Source: MAME mame0289 (commit f34f02505e32), src/mame/atari/nl_tank.cpp,
# NETLIST_START(tank). Licence BSD-3-Clause by the file's own header (line 1),
# copyright-holders Ryan Holtz (line 2).
# https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mamedev/mame/mame0289/src/mame/atari/nl_tank.cpp
# Converted by tools/mame_netlist.py; checked by tools/build_board_nets.py.
#
# What the conversion means. MAME's netlists are written to be simulated, so this is a
# second reading of the sheet by someone else, not a read of it: designators and pin
# numbers are MAME's unless the notes say the sheet was read to correct them. Names on
# `label` lines are MAME's, which mostly follow the sheet's with Q for an overbar; `net`
# is used only for the supply rails. A `port` is a net that leaves what this file
# describes -- a signal from the CPU or the other board, a cabinet control, or a source
# MAME simulates with a stand-in rather than the circuit.
#
#   net NAME: PIN ...     a supply rail
#   label NAME: PIN ...   a net MAME names
#   wire PIN PIN ...      an unnamed connection
#   port NAME: PIN ...    a net that leaves this file (see above)
#   nc PIN ...            a pin with nothing attached
#   parallel PIN ...      outputs the board sums on one node by design
#   value REF VALUE       a passive's value, in the unit MAME's own macro uses
#
# PIN is DESIGNATOR.NUMBER. Diode pin 1 is the cathode; transistors keep B, C and E;
# MAME does not record which way round an electrolytic goes, so C pins are MAME's 1/2.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Undone: what MAME does to simulate the board that the board does not do
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# line 357: dropped NET_C(IC_B6.2, IC_B6.6, IC_D6.9) -- MAME's 7400 latch; Board I sheet 2 draws a 7404 pair (below)
# line 358: dropped NET_C(IC_B6.4, IC_B6.3, IC_N6.5) -- as above
# line 359: dropped NET_C(IC_B6.12, IC_B6.8, IC_D6.8) -- as above
# line 360: dropped NET_C(IC_B6.10, IC_B6.11, IC_N6.6) -- as above
# line 376: dropped NET_C(GND, IC_D6.3) -- the 25c/50c switch in its 25c position; the switch is put back (SW1)
# line 382: dropped NET_C(PLAYTIME.1, R54A.1, R53A.1) -- took R53A.1 out of it: R53 is switched in by the 25c/50c switch (SW2), not fixed
# line 395: dropped NET_C(V5, IC_E6.10) -- 'No antenna to spark, so we pretend we never get a spark'; the antenna latch is put back
# line 400: dropped NET_C(GND, IC_N6.8) -- as above
# line 1494: dropped NET_C(VLD1, IC_M2.1, IC_M2.2) -- Board I sheet 1 puts /FIRE1 on M2 pins 1-2 and VLD1 on 13
# line 1495: dropped NET_C(FIRE1Q, IC_M2.13) -- as above
# line 1499: dropped NET_C(HMCE, IC_F2.12, IC_F2.5, IC_F2.9, IC_C1.1) -- Board I makes its own HMCE from /HMCE with J3 pins 9-8; MAME takes Board II's
# line 1500: dropped NET_C(IC_D2.5, IC_F2.13) -- Board I sheet 1: D2.5 goes to F2.12
# line 1501: dropped NET_C(IC_E2.5, IC_F2.4) -- Board I sheet 1: E2.5 goes to F2.5
# line 1502: dropped NET_C(IC_D2.9, IC_F2.10) -- Board I sheet 1: the 2^3 latch D2.9 goes to C1.1 (the NAND), not F2
# line 1503: dropped NET_C(IC_E2.9, IC_C1.2) -- Board I sheet 1: the 2^2 latch E2.9 goes to F2.9, not C1
# line 1506: dropped NET_C(EXPL1Q, IC_C1.5) -- Board I takes /EXPL1 from its own J3.12, not Board II's
# line 1630: dropped NET_C(HMCE, IC_F4.1, IC_F4.4, IC_F4.10, IC_C5.4) -- as for line 1499
# line 1662: dropped NET_C(EXPL2Q, IC_C5.2) -- Board I takes /EXPL2 from its own H3.10, not Board II's
# line 1748: dropped NET_C(R71A.2, C40A.1, HLE_NOISE.1) -- a random-noise stand-in; the noise transistor Q5 is put back
# line 1750: dropped NET_C(GND, HLE_NOISE.2, C43A.2, R73A.2, C38A.1) -- took HLE_NOISE.2 out of it: as above
# line 1761: dropped NET_C(C31A.2, IC_K6.2) -- C31 feeds K6's input (MFC6040 pin 3); MAME puts it on the control pin
# line 1884: dropped NET_C(C101.2, GND) -- on to VOLUME 1 and the LM380 amplifier, which MAME does not have; MAME grounds it
# line 1885: dropped NET_C(C106.2, GND) -- on to VOLUME 2 and the second LM380, likewise
# line 1905: NET_C(GND, IC_A6.11, IC_A6.13) -> nc -- tied to GND in MAME's "Unused Gates / Pins" block
# line 1906: NET_C(GND, IC_N6.11, IC_N6.12) -> nc -- tied to GND in MAME's "Unused Gates / Pins" block
# line 1904: MAME ties UN4.1, UN4.3 off as unused, but the circuit uses them -- the tie is dropped
# line 1905: MAME ties UA6.13 off as unused, but the circuit uses them -- the tie is dropped
# line 1910: MAME ties UJ3.9 off as unused, but the circuit uses them -- the tie is dropped
# lines 1797-1833: restored from a comment -- the Motor 1 sound, which MAME comments out; compared with Board II sheet 1 and corrected below
# lines 1837-1872: restored from a comment -- the Motor 2 sound, likewise
#
# Corrected from the sheet (the notes below say what was read where):
#   UB6: the sheet's part is 7404, MAME's 7400 -- Board I sheet 2: two cross-coupled inverter pairs, not NAND latches
#   UK6: the sheet's part is MFC6040, MAME's MC3340 -- Board I sheet 2 prints MFC6040; its pin numbers differ from the MC3340's, so MAME's pins are mapped onto it
#   UL6: the sheet's part is MFC6040, MAME's MC3340 -- Board I sheet 2 prints MFC6040; pins mapped as for K6
#   UA6: the sheet's part is 74H04, MAME's 7404 -- Board I sheet 1 prints H04
#   UM1: the sheet's part is 74S20, MAME's 7420 -- Board I sheet 1 prints S20
#   UM5: the sheet's part is 74S20, MAME's 7420 -- Board I sheet 1 prints S20
#   UM3: the sheet's part is 74H08, MAME's 7408 -- Board I sheet 1 prints H08
#   R53: the sheet's value is 330K, MAME's 220K -- Board I sheet 2 rev J, and rev G
#   parts the sheet draws that MAME does not have: Q1 2N3643, C15 0.1uF, C16 0.1uF, C17 0.1uF, CR9 1N914, CR12 1N914, R41 4.7K, R42 100K, R49 1K, R101 1K, R100 100, Q40 2N3643, Q41 2N5190, SW1 25c/50c (coin logic), SW2 25c/50c (play time), R48 560, Q5 2N3643 (selected noise transistor)
#   Board I sheet 2: coin 1 NC (J3-13) on B6.13, cross-coupled with B6.10: UB6.13 UB6.10 UD6.9 (COIN1_NC)
#   Board I sheet 2: coin 1 NO (J3-14) on B6.11, cross-coupled with B6.12: UB6.11 UB6.12 UN6.5 (COIN1_NO)
#   Board I sheet 2: coin 2 NO (J3-12) on B6.5, cross-coupled with B6.2: UB6.5 UB6.2 UN6.6 (COIN2_NO)
#   Board I sheet 2: coin 2 NC (J3-11) on B6.1, cross-coupled with B6.6: UB6.1 UB6.6 UD6.8 (COIN2_NC)
#   Board I sheet 2: the 25c/50c switch, which MAME hard-wires in the 25c position. Not designated on the sheet; SW1/SW2 are ours: UD6.3 SW1.1 R48.1; R48.2 SW1.2; UN6.1 SW1.3; R53.1 SW2.1; VR1.1 SW2.2
#   Board I sheet 2: the antenna circuit MAME replaces with a tie: C17.1 (ANT); C17.2 CR12.K R42.1 C16.2 Q1.B; CR12.A R42.2 CR9.K C15.2; R49.1; R49.2 C15.1 C16.1; Q1.E CR9.A; Q1.C UN4.1 R41.1; UN4.2 UN4.3 UN6.8; UN4.4 R41.2 UE6.10
#   Board I sheet 2: the coin counter driver, which MAME does not draw: UD6.10 UA6.13; UA6.12 R101.1; R101.2 Q40.B; R100.1; R100.2 Q40.C; Q40.E Q41.B; Q41.C (COIN_COUNTER); Q41.E (TV_GROUND)
#   Board I sheet 2: Q5's emitter is the noise source; base and collector grounded: R71.2 C40.1 Q5.E
#   as above: Q5.B Q5.C
#   Board I sheet 2: C31 into K6 pin 3: C31.2 UK6.3
#   Board I sheet 1: UD2.5 UF2.12; UE2.5 UF2.5; UE2.9 UF2.9; UD2.9 UC1.1; UM2.13; UM2.1 UM2.2
#   Board I sheet 1: HMCE, inverted on the board from /HMCE (J1-25): UJ3.8 UF2.13 UF2.4 UF2.10 UC1.2 UF4.1 UF4.4 UF4.10 UC5.4 (HMCE_B1)
#   Board I sheet 1: /HMCE in from J1-25: UJ3.9
#   Board I sheet 1: /EXPL1 from J3.12: UJ3.12 UC1.5
#   Board I sheet 1: /EXPL2 from H3.10: UH3.10 UC5.2
# line 1093: RVID is not a part -- MAME's 10K to ground standing in for the monitor's input
# line 1830: R555OUT1 is not a part -- a 1K to ground on the 555's output, which the sheet leaves undrawn
# line 1869: R555OUT2 is not a part -- a 1K to ground on the 555's output, which the sheet leaves undrawn
# Stand-ins that are not parts (the nets they drive are ports): SWITCH(P1_LEFT_UP), SWITCH(P1_LEFT_DOWN), SWITCH(P1_RIGHT_UP), SWITCH(P1_RIGHT_DOWN), SWITCH(P1_FIRE), SWITCH(P2_LEFT_UP), SWITCH(P2_LEFT_DOWN), SWITCH(P2_RIGHT_UP), SWITCH(P2_RIGHT_DOWN), SWITCH(P2_FIRE), SWITCH2(COIN1), SWITCH2(COIN2), CLOCK(CLK), CLOCK(NOISE_CLOCK)
#
# Left out by MAME (commented out at TAG, so not in this file either):
#   line 158: CAP(C34A, CAP_U(0.01)) Decoupling
#   line 1090: RES(RPROBE, 220)
#
# Compared with both Board I sheets in full (003110 rev J; rev H and rev G for faint spots),
# 2026-10-19. MAME agrees with the sheet on the tank motion counters and their presets
# (B1/B5 3-5 to P and 6 grounded; C2/C4/J1/J5 4 grounded), the clock inverters on A6, F3
# and the WINDO outputs, the shell counters and the 2^7 latches cleared by /EXPL, shell 2's
# latch routing, the shell and blast output gating, the coin flip-flops apart from B6, and
# the play timer, noise, shot and boom values apart from R53. Its errors here, all corrected
# above: B6 is a 7404, not a 7400; K6 and L6 are MFC6040s, whose pins are not the MC3340's;
# C31 feeds K6's input, not its control pin; R53 is 330K; shell 1's 2^2 and 2^3 latches are
# crossed between the F2 and C1 gates; M2's inputs are swapped (electrically the same NAND);
# and Board I makes its own HMCE, /EXPL1 and /EXPL2 from what the cable brings, where MAME
# takes Board II's. MAME's antenna tie, 25c hard-wiring, unused-input ties on N4 and A6 (the
# antenna latch and the coin counter use them) and grounded mixer outputs are undone.
#
# Open questions, each as printed and not settled:
# * The cable. This sheet prints VLD1 on J1-9 and /FIRE1 on J1-24; Board II's prints
#   FIRE1-bar on J4-9 and VLD1 on J4-24. Every other contact agrees pin for pin, and the
#   only Board I load (M2, a 3-input NAND of both) cannot tell them apart. Each board is
#   given its own sheet's contact.
# * J6's second 7474 half is printed "J4" on rev H and rev J (pins 1-6, the coin latch). J4
#   is a 9316 on sheet 1; MAME calls this half J6, and so does this file.
# * BOOM COM reaches Q6 through two series 1N914s, both labelled CR22. MAME has one CR22;
#   this file follows MAME.
# * M1's first gate prints input "3" (MAME, and tank 2's M5, use 5); L3 prints an input
#   "10" that is its own output (MAME uses 8); N1 and N5 print their /CLR numbers swapped
#   (both go to /HRST, so it is harmless). MAME's pins are kept.
# * SW1 and SW2 are the 25c/50c switch as drawn in two places; whether they are two poles of
#   one switch is not on the sheet. The 50c contact of SW2 is drawn unconnected.
#
# Ours, not printed: UX1 (the noise amplifier's 741, which has no grid position), VR1-VR3
# (the PLAY TIME pot and the shot and boom noise pots), SW1, SW2. Not in this file: the
# +5V, +12V and -12V supplies and the two LM380 amplifiers with their volume pots, which are
# on sheet 2 and not in MAME; OUT1 and OUT2 are where the mixers hand over to them.

